* Constant On-Time Lab -- low-bandwidth two-phase average-current balancer
* Current monitor inputs use 1 V/A. Positive TRIM is intended to be added to
* the phase feedback signal, reducing that phase's future pulse requests.

* CURRENT_BALANCE_2 I1 I2 ENABLE TRIM1 TRIM2 ERROR
.SUBCKT CURRENT_BALANCE_2 I1 I2 ENABLE TRIM1 TRIM2 ERROR PARAMS:
+ BW=5k CAVG=10n KBAL=20m TRIMMAX=100m VLOGIC=1
RAVG1 I1 IAVG1 {1/(6.283185307*BW*CAVG)}
CAVG1 IAVG1 0 {CAVG} IC=0
RAVG2 I2 IAVG2 {1/(6.283185307*BW*CAVG)}
CAVG2 IAVG2 0 {CAVG} IC=0
EERROR ERROR 0 VALUE={V(IAVG1)-V(IAVG2)}
EENABLE EN01 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(ENABLE)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
ETRIM1 TRIM1 0 VALUE={V(EN01)*LIMIT(KBAL*V(ERROR)/2,
+ -TRIMMAX,TRIMMAX)}
ETRIM2 TRIM2 0 VALUE={-V(EN01)*LIMIT(KBAL*V(ERROR)/2,
+ -TRIMMAX,TRIMMAX)}
RERROR ERROR 0 1G
RTRIM1 TRIM1 0 1G
RTRIM2 TRIM2 0 1G
.ENDS CURRENT_BALANCE_2

* Reusable cell for a generated N-phase current balancer. The caller computes
* IREFERENCE from the active phases' filtered IAVG outputs. Positive phase
* error produces positive TRIM, which is added to feedback and reduces that
* phase's future pulse demand. ENABLE is normalized with VLOGIC.
* CURRENT_BALANCE_CELL ISENSE IREFERENCE ENABLE IAVG TRIM ERROR
.SUBCKT CURRENT_BALANCE_CELL ISENSE IREFERENCE ENABLE IAVG TRIM ERROR PARAMS:
+ BW=5k CAVG=10n KBAL=20m TRIMMAX=100m VLOGIC=1
RAVG ISENSE IAVGINT {1/(6.283185307*BW*CAVG)}
CAVGF IAVGINT 0 {CAVG} IC=0
EIAVG IAVG 0 VALUE={V(IAVGINT)}
EERROR ERROR 0 VALUE={V(IAVGINT)-V(IREFERENCE)}
EENABLE EN01 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(ENABLE)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
ETRIM TRIM 0 VALUE={V(EN01)*LIMIT(KBAL*V(ERROR),
+ -TRIMMAX,TRIMMAX)}
RIAVG IAVG 0 1G
RERROR ERROR 0 1G
RTRIM TRIM 0 1G
.ENDS CURRENT_BALANCE_CELL
